{
 "source": {
  "repository": "OpenPresentation/opf-pptx",
  "commit": "438ce8801701f2fa2531ac56537234d274e36aa7",
  "note": "RR-54: toPptx bytes of chart and table decks that use none of the RR-54 fields (no DataColumn objects, datasets, mapping, source or formats, and only strict-decimal or number chart cells), from main before RR-54 (re-pinned to main 4ca079f, the pptxgenjs-plus 4.3.4 migration of opf-pptx#165, whose output change the owner approved). The RR-54 export must keep these bytes exactly. Regenerate only with an owner decision to change the default export. FA-03: the stacked and percent-stacked entries name the clean chart type ids (no -3x suffix), so their titles and tags, and so their bytes, changed; every other entry is unchanged. FA-23 (OPF 0.15, owner-approved breaking spec): every entry regenerated: with zero built-in catalog records the engine-default colour scheme is written as clrScheme name=\"OpenPresentation\" (0.14 named the built-in cool-horizon record \"Cool Horizon\"), and chartex-native-map names the world chart type, since map is no 0.15 chart type. Generated on the FA-20 + FA-22 core branches with zero built-ins; re-run at integration with the released core 0.15. RR-59: the three entries with a table (table, styled-table, mixed-blocks) are repinned because full provenance now records every inline table as authored (the OPF_DATA_V1 tag); previousSha256 keeps the FA-23 hash and nativeSlideSha256 locks the slide XML without its customer-data tags, which is unchanged. RR-59 (AUTO-18, round trip restores absent document defaults): full provenance now records the document-level defaults a document leaves to the engine (OPF_DOCUMENT_V1.absent), so every full-mode export carries the document tag and its slide tags, also when the document states nothing else. Verified part by part against a build of main 3d2698f: with the OPF_DOCUMENT_V1 and OPF_SLIDE_V1 tag parts, their relationships, content-type overrides and custDataLst references removed, every package is byte-identical to main; only the tag parts changed."
 },
